    "native_visual_review_evidence": "KM821 native source and final preview review\n\nReviewed original native source, header000 KM821, vertical KM821 footer, all30 blocks, all49 input terminals, every printed output, literal function/unit/card/location/grid field, border wedge, input prefix, caption, route, diamond, unjoined crossing and footer field. Final complete JuliaMono preview compared to original overview and native enlarged channel/gate/footer crops; AN final pin crop reviewed after its row correction. No unreadable printed glyphs remain.\n\nNative corrections retained:\nAB.B09 drives AD.D12 via c91; external invalid-instruction source owns c92, AG.B09 diamond and AH.B07. BG.D02 owns AH.B05 and upper KM191/AN.B08 bridge. AP export is the native row28 invalid-address-priority signal. AN B13/B08 are rows20/21, aligned with card/location fields.\nLower distinct rails: RR00 c112 to BB.B13; RX-format c113 to AZ.B04; AM forced c114 to AS.D11 and AZ.B03/BA.B07/BB.B10; AX c115 to AS.D12 and AZ.B05/BA.B09/BB.B12. Source-native wedged AX.B03 preserved; no commoning or inferred joins.\nAM source literal function ✲A is inside the box and its second input is an unnamed wedge. BF printed prefix8 and physical pinD12 are separately recorded. AU and BA source literal F-C3E3 differs from A1 E-C3E3; native fields retained with documented index discrepancies.\nThree below-row source references and c41 upward stubs retained. Native ordinary bends recalibrated to block borders and printed pin adjacency; no bank departure. All four printed captions, header, continuation rows, 11-06-69 date, LOG018A, 2585092 part number, SDD BLK. BK, and revisions08-08-69 713380/10-16-69 713383 independently reviewed. P.N. label follows the explicit human footer convention.\n"
